<!--
The usage strings below are written into Info.plist by scripts/prepare-native.mjs
on the iOS build machine. They do not turn Tap to Pay on.

Do not add com.apple.developer.proximity-reader.payment.acceptance to the
signed iOS build until Apple grants it. Adding the entitlement before
approval makes the archive fail to sign. Do not submit that request from
the app or from this file.

When Apple approves it:
1. Add the entitlement to the App ID and the app's entitlements file.
2. Set TAP_TO_PAY_IOS_ENABLED to true in src/lib/tapToPay.ts.
3. The in-app onboarding screens are already in the app. Payment stays off until the flag is true.

NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription
Dispatch uses your location to check you in at job sites and to take a card payment with Tap to Pay on iPhone.

NFCReaderUsageDescription
Dispatch uses NFC so a customer can tap a card on this iPhone.
-->
